6)Monolithic vs Microservices Architecture

Monolithic Architecture is a type of architecture which is developed as an indivisible unit and is deployed as a single unit. Everything is tightly coupled.
The disadvantage here is that any updates in any one of the structure meant deploying the whole application again. It also has a single database. But , it has simple
architecture but gives scalability issues.

Microservice Architecture is kind of loose architecture which helps in scalibility and flexibility. And easy to maintain. 
